[Rotproof](https://github.com/secta113/rotproof) keeps the layers and the records in `docs/`. It is pinned in
`package.json`, and CI (`.github/workflows/ci.yml`) installs it with `npm ci` and runs `rotproof check`. Pin it once,
with the version that made this project:

```sh
npm install -D -E rotproof@{version}
npx --no -- rotproof check
```

npm installs the binary for your platform with it (Windows x64 or Linux x64). Your agent's hooks run
`rotproof time-hook`, which has to be on the `PATH` they run with: `node_modules/.bin` is not, so install the same
version there too (`npm install -g rotproof@{version}`), or put `node_modules/.bin` on the `PATH` your agent starts
with.
